WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
MCP systems can move sensitive data through prompts, resources, files, logs,

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.360
retrieval results, tool responses, and downstream APIs.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.720
That makes data protection a first-class design concern.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.145
A model context may include customer records, internal documents, code, tickets,

00:00:15.145 --> 00:00:18.555
telemetry, credentials, regulated information, or personal data.

00:00:18.555 --> 00:00:22.395
The fact that the data is being used to help the user does not remove the need for access

00:00:22.395 --> 00:00:22.705
control,

00:00:22.705 --> 00:00:25.520
minimization, retention limits, and monitoring.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.610
Resource access should be governed by application policy and identity,

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:29.880
not by model confidence.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.705
If a user is not allowed to read a document,

00:00:31.705 --> 00:00:34.636
the model should not receive that document because it seems useful.

00:00:34.636 --> 00:00:37.995
Per-user access filtering, tenant isolation, group membership checks,

00:00:37.995 --> 00:00:43.265
and resource-level permissions should happen before content enters the model context.

00:00:43.265 --> 00:00:47.335
Cross-user or cross-tenant leakage is a severe failure because the model may summarize,

00:00:47.335 --> 00:00:50.910
combine, or expose information that never should have been available.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.960
Resource provenance helps teams reason about trust.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.790
The system should know where content came from, when it was retrieved,

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:59.531
which identity accessed it, and whether it is authoritative for the current task.

00:00:59.531 --> 00:01:04.045
Stale or untrusted resources should not silently drive high-impact actions.

00:01:04.045 --> 00:01:06.895
Redaction can reduce exposure when full content is unnecessary.

00:01:06.895 --> 00:01:11.750
Data minimization asks whether the model needs the whole file, a small excerpt, metadata,

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:14.350
or a structured result from a server-side query.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.080
Secrets handling deserves special care.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.470
Tokens, credentials, private keys, session cookies,

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:22.775
and connection strings should not be placed in prompts, tool descriptions, or logs.

00:01:22.775 --> 00:01:26.413
Local file access should be constrained to intended paths and operations.

00:01:26.413 --> 00:01:29.730
Cloud resource access should use least privilege and service-side policy.

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:32.680
Encryption, retention controls, and logging hygiene matter,

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:34.440
but they do not replace authorization.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:38.840
MCP data protection works best when sensitive content is filtered before it reaches the

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:39.040
model.
